35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found the ledger! Seventy percent of costs are fixed, like hall hire, even if nobody comes. That’s huge!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The data confirms my fears. Turnout dropped a third after door charges, and quiet members feel uneasy about per-event costs.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, the sheets prove it. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the work. Eighteen people never show up. It’s unfair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The logs show six hours monthly chasing individual payments, versus one for yearly. Eleven mid-year joiners required manual calculations. The administrative burden is unsustainable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, the forms show people fear a whole-year commitment. The quiet members feel uneasy about per-event costs. We need a structure that feels safe and flexible, not just cheap.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, six hours a month chasing money? That’s exhausting! I’m glad we’re not doing that. @Jonathan, does that mean flat fees are safer for everyone?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, not necessarily. The data shows people stopped feeling ownership when we charged per event. A flat fee might feel like a tax, not a belonging.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, it’s not just about chasing money. It’s that the same nine people do everything while eighteen pay and vanish. That’s the real problem.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, the manual calculations for mid-year joiners are a hidden cost. We need a structure that minimizes this administrative friction for the next treasurer.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mio, I agree. The fear of a big upfront commitment is real. We need a way for people to drift in without feeling trapped by a whole year’s cost.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Jonathan, that makes sense! If a flat fee feels like a tax, maybe we need a middle ground? I just want everyone to feel welcome, not just paying!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, perhaps. The hesitation suggests people need to feel the fee buys belonging, not just access. I’ll wait for the options to see if any fit that.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, a middle ground won’t fix the rot. The same nine are burning out while eighteen ghost. We need to see who’s actually carrying the weight before we pick a fee.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the burnout is real, but the administrative load is the immediate crisis. I need a system that doesn’t break the next person.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
